# Ownership, and therefore who must approve a pull request.
#
# LAST MATCHING RULE WINS in CODEOWNERS. The `*` line comes first so it is the fallback;
# every rule below it is more specific and overrides it for those paths.
#
# Branch protection is configured "Require review from Code Owners" with 1 approval, and
# "Do not allow bypassing" is deliberately OFF. Because a PR author can never approve their
# own PR, the sole code owner would otherwise be permanently blocked on his own changes. So:
#
#   @tyler-technologies/onetyler-tcp-pm-admins        admin  -> can merge without review
#   @tyler-technologies/onetyler-tcp-pm-contributors  write  -> PRs need approval
#
# Put reviewers on the CONTRIBUTORS team. Adding someone to the admins team silently removes
# the review requirement from them, which is the opposite of the intent.

*                               @vijay-tylertech

# =======================================================================================
# ADMIN-ONLY — team-level routing, and how the repo operates
# =======================================================================================
# Mirrors .github/admin-only-paths.txt, which CI and the session script read. The two
# CANNOT share a file (this is GitHub's own format), so scripts/check_admin_paths.py
# asserts they agree and CI runs it. If you change one, change both.
#
# The boundary: contributors own subject-matter content; admins own anything that decides
# WHICH AGENT answers. A bad knowledge edit gives one wrong answer. A bad routing edit
# misroutes every conversation, and the transcript that reveals it looks like a content
# problem.

# --- team-level routing ---
/README.md                      @vijay-tylertech
/team-config/                   @vijay-tylertech
# Per-corpus start pages look like within-corpus routing, and partly are. But they also
# carry CROSS-AGENT hand-off rules — Knowledge-BP-General/_START_HERE.md opens by telling
# the agent to decide whether a question belongs to one of the four specialized agents, and
# routes to Identity / Ops Center / SAC by name. CODEOWNERS cannot own half a file, so the
# whole file is admin-owned.
/Knowledge-*/_START_HERE.md     @vijay-tylertech

