# =======================================================================================
# CONTRIBUTOR-EDITABLE
# =======================================================================================
# Knowledge CONTENT in each corpus — the Conf-, Docusaurus-, FAQ-, Misc-, Training- and
# GitHub- files — is where contributors are expected to work. That is the point of having
# them: they know the subject matter.
#
# These paths are still owned (so every PR gets an approval — branch protection requires one
# regardless), but ownership is recorded here as the contributors team to say plainly that
# this is their ground. The `_START_HERE.md` rule above is MORE specific than these folder
# rules, so it still wins for that one file in each folder.
#
# NOTE the limit of path-based enforcement: nothing here stops a contributor putting
# team-level routing advice INSIDE a knowledge file — "for identity questions use the
# Identity agent" in an FAQ is routing content in a file they may edit. No tool catches
# that. Human review is the only control, so read content edits for routing claims.
/Knowledge-OpsCenter/           @tyler-technologies/onetyler-tcp-pm-contributors
/Knowledge-BP-General/          @tyler-technologies/onetyler-tcp-pm-contributors
/Knowledge-SupportAccessCenter/ @tyler-technologies/onetyler-tcp-pm-contributors
/Knowledge-TylerIdentity/       @tyler-technologies/onetyler-tcp-pm-contributors
/Knowledge-AlignedReleases/     @tyler-technologies/onetyler-tcp-pm-contributors
/Knowledge-StatusPageAndSLA/    @tyler-technologies/onetyler-tcp-pm-contributors
/Knowledge-Shared/              @tyler-technologies/onetyler-tcp-pm-contributors

# Re-stated AFTER the folder rules because last-match-wins: without these, the folder rules
# above would hand the start pages back to the contributors team.
/Knowledge-*/_START_HERE.md     @vijay-tylertech

